{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.94,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["U3"],
      "pins": ["U3.1", "U3.2", "U3.3", "U3.4", "U3.5", "U3.6"],
      "nets": ["+3V3", "VBUS", "GND", "Net-(U3-SW)", "Net-(U3-BST)"],
      "observed": "The AP63203WU is wired according to a pin assignment that does not match the device's physical pinout: U3.1 (FB) is on +3V3, U3.2 (EN) and U3.3 (IN) are on VBUS, U3.4 (GND) is on GND, U3.5 (SW) is on Net-(U3-SW), and U3.6 (BST) is on Net-(U3-BST). The AP63203WU physical pinout is 1=BST, 2=GND, 3=SW, 4=IN, 5=EN, 6=FB.",
      "expected": "For the AP63203WU, physical pin 1 should connect to the bootstrap capacitor, pin 2 to GND, pin 3 to the switching node, pin 4 to VBUS, pin 5 to the enable supply, and pin 6 to the 3.3 V feedback/output. The current pin-number mapping instead places VBUS on physical GND and GND on physical IN, so the regulator will not produce the intended 3.3 V rail.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U3\") (value \"AP63203WU\") (footprint \"Package_TO_SOT_SMD:TSOT-23-6\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"FB\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"EN\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"IN\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"SW\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"BST\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"VBUS\") (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"2\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"3\"))) (net (name \"GND\") (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"4\"))) (net (name \"+3V3\") (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "AP63203WU ... is the part actually driving the 3.3 V rail."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The regulator's physical ground and input pins are connected to the wrong rails, and the other control and power pins are also misassigned. The board is therefore unlikely to generate a valid 3.3 V supply, preventing normal operation of the MCU and other logic.",
      "confidence": 0.94
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The AP63203WU symbol/netlist pin numbering does not match the part's physical pinout. As wired, the regulator's physical GND pin receives VBUS and its physical IN pin receives GND, so the intended 3.3 V rail is compromised."
}

